{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/suffixstructures\/suffixtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every suffix of every text ends at a leaf, the empty suffix included, and every internal node","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a point where suffixes that agree so far go different ways, so the tree has at most 2","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nodes. A pattern is found in O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") steps down from the root, and the leaves below where it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends are its occurrences.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let tree = SuffixTree(\"banana\")","tree.occurrences(of: \"ana\").map(\\.range)   \/\/ [3 ..< 6, 1 ..< 4]","tree.longestRepeatedSubstring?.range       \/\/ 3 ..< 6, \"ana\"","","let both = SuffixTree(texts: [\"xabxac\", \"abcabxabcd\"])","both.longestCommonSubstring                \/\/ text 1, 3 ..< 7: \"abxa\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nodes are numbered in preorder from the root at 0, so a node’s subtree is the nodes from it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"just before the next node that is not its descendant. Children come in the order of the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that starts their edge: sorted when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", so the leaves are in the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their suffixes and match a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of the same text; otherwise in the order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols first occur in the texts. Each text ends in a terminator of its own that sorts before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every symbol and belongs to no label."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tree converts to Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and its suffix links are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a directed graph, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Each node takes 32 bytes and each symbol 4 more, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"texts’ codes, which the tree keeps."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/Occurrence","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/d